Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns in alien_data and their potential usage  
• state: grouping aliens to find population per state, calculate top 10 states  
• aggressive: classify aliens as “friendly” (0) or “hostile” (1) and compute percentages  
• age: compute average age of aliens by state and filter states whose average age > 200  
• id (or any other unique column): just for counting aliens (COUNT(*))  

Below are ten step‑by‑step SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows) that progressively explore the data and finally answer the question.  
All of them refer only to the alien_data table.

```sql
-- 1. Description: List a few distinct U.S. states represented in the alien_data table
SELECT DISTINCT "state"
FROM "alien_data"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Show a head‑count of aliens per state, ordered from largest to smallest
SELECT "state",
       COUNT(*) AS "alien_population"
FROM   "alien_data"
GROUP  BY "state"
ORDER  BY "alien_population" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Retrieve just the TOP 10 states by alien population
WITH pop AS (
  SELECT "state",
         COUNT(*) AS "alien_population"
  FROM   "alien_data"
  GROUP  BY "state"
  ORDER  BY "alien_population" DESC
  LIMIT 10
)
SELECT *
FROM   pop
ORDER  BY "alien_population" DESC;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Friendly (aggressive = 0) vs. hostile (aggressive = 1) counts for every state
SELECT "state",
       SUM(CASE WHEN "aggressive" = 0 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS "friendly_cnt",
       SUM(CASE WHEN "aggressive" = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS "hostile_cnt"
FROM   "alien_data"
GROUP  BY "state"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Calculate friendly and hostile PERCENTAGES for each state
SELECT "state",
       100.0 * SUM(CASE WHEN "aggressive" = 0 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) /
              COUNT(*) AS "friendly_pct",
       100.0 * SUM(CASE WHEN "aggressive" = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) /
              COUNT(*) AS "hostile_pct"
FROM   "alien_data"
GROUP  BY "state"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Add average age to the friendly/hostile percentage breakdown
SELECT "state",
       AVG("age") AS "avg_age",
       100.0 * SUM(CASE WHEN "aggressive" = 0 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) / COUNT(*) AS "friendly_pct",
       100.0 * SUM(CASE WHEN "aggressive" = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) / COUNT(*) AS "hostile_pct"
FROM   "alien_data"
GROUP  BY "state"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Keep only states where friendly_pct > hostile_pct
SELECT "state",
       AVG("age")         AS "avg_age",
       COUNT(*)           AS "alien_population"
FROM   "alien_data"
GROUP  BY "state"
HAVING 100.0 * SUM(CASE WHEN "aggressive" = 0 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) / COUNT(*) >
       100.0 * SUM(CASE WHEN "aggressive" = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) / COUNT(*)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Add the requirement that the average age is greater than 200
SELECT "state",
       AVG("age")         AS "avg_age",
       COUNT(*)           AS "alien_population"
FROM   "alien_data"
GROUP  BY "state"
HAVING AVG("age") > 200
   AND 100.0 * SUM(CASE WHEN "aggressive" = 0 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) / COUNT(*) >
       100.0 * SUM(CASE WHEN "aggressive" = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) / COUNT(*)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Combine everything—filter to TOP 10 population states first, then apply both conditions
WITH top10 AS (
  SELECT "state"
  FROM   "alien_data"
  GROUP  BY "state"
  ORDER  BY COUNT(*) DESC
  LIMIT 10
)
SELECT a."state",
       AVG(a."age") AS "avg_age"
FROM   "alien_data" AS a
JOIN   top10        AS t ON a."state" = t."state"
GROUP  BY a."state"
HAVING AVG(a."age") > 200
   AND 100.0 * SUM(CASE WHEN a."aggressive" = 0 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) / COUNT(*) >
       100.0 * SUM(CASE WHEN a."aggressive" = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) / COUNT(*)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: FINAL answer – count how many of those TOP‑10 states satisfy the two requirements
WITH top10 AS (
  SELECT "state"
  FROM   "alien_data"
  GROUP  BY "state"
  ORDER  BY COUNT(*) DESC
  LIMIT 10
),
qualified AS (
  SELECT a."state"
  FROM   "alien_data" AS a
  JOIN   top10        AS t ON a."state" = t."state"
  GROUP  BY a."state"
  HAVING AVG(a."age") > 200
     AND 100.0 * SUM(CASE WHEN a."aggressive" = 0 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) / COUNT(*) >
         100.0 * SUM(CASE WHEN a."aggressive" = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) / COUNT(*)
)
SELECT COUNT(*) AS "num_states_meeting_criteria"
FROM   qualified;
```

